theorem sum-formula
  metamath    arisum
  let n ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  then S(n) = n(n + 1)/2

1.  S(n) = n(n + 1)/2
    induction on n starting at 1, from H1

    base
    1.1.  S(1) = 1
          def:stdlib/sums/S

    1.2.  S(1) = 1(1 + 1)/2
          calculation
            S(1) = 1                 1.1
                 = 1(1 + 1)/2        arithmetic

    step
    1.3.  For every k ∈ ℕ, if S(k) = k(k + 1)/2
          then S(k + 1) = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2.
          fix
          let k ∈ ℕ                                                   (K)
          assume S(k) = k(k + 1)/2                                    (IH)

          1.3.1.  S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)
                  def:stdlib/sums/S n := k, from K

          1.3.2.  S(k) + (k + 1) = k(k + 1)/2 + (k + 1)
                  substitute S(k) = k(k + 1)/2 (IH)

          1.3.3.  k(k + 1)/2 + (k + 1) = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2
                  algebra
                  requires 2 ≠ 0: arithmetic
                  requires k ∈ ℝ: thm:stdlib/numbers/nat-real, from K

          1.3.4.  S(k + 1) = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2
                  calculation
                    S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)               1.3.1
                             = k(k + 1)/2 + (k + 1)         1.3.2
                             = (k + 1)((k + 1) + 1)/2       1.3.3
